Fix suggest_url in policies. r=Standard8, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D131291", "files": ["browser/components/enterprisepolicies/Policies.jsm", "browser/components/enterprisepolicies/tests/browser/browser_policy_search_engine.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "1768594a837b828f4dadaa0363f32dd0964edf4a", "parents": ["2e12bb19f86653071e6b9f6760194f09cd4a5bca"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Mark Smith \u003cmcs@pearlcrescent.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1586061: Prevent additional hidden windows from being created if one already exists on macOS. r=mstange, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D134055", "files": ["xpfe/appshell/nsAppShellService.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "aecc104f3229dcdbccada09f52e9f7a07cddfe40", "parents": ["1768594a837b828f4dadaa0363f32dd0964edf4a"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Edgar Chen \u003cechen@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1739220 - Handle fullscreen state in a more reliable way; r=smaug,Gijs, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D131185", "files": ["browser/actors/DOMFullscreenChild.jsm", "browser/actors/DOMFullscreenParent.jsm", "browser/base/content/browser-fullScreenAndPointerLock.js"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "aff97ff1564d15a114922f6f25ae0687cde504f5", "parents": ["aecc104f3229dcdbccada09f52e9f7a07cddfe40"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1746530 - Save and restore previous FBO in SwCompositor::create_tile. r=jrmuizel, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D134131", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/compositor/sw_compositor.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "453c6d45269bb39aa0e58afa7942d0aa5cec49bc", "parents": ["aff97ff1564d15a114922f6f25ae0687cde504f5"], "tags": []}], "date": 1640096072, "git_changesets": [null, null, null, null, null, null, null, null], "user": "ryanvm@gmail.com"}, "130": {"changesets": [{"author": "Butkovits Atila \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1729487 - disable browser_storage_fission_session_storage.js on Linux_debug for frequent failures. a=RyanVM. DONTBUILD", "files": ["devtools/client/storage/test/browser.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "32173ce051143f88f26c0888fb164b3c4c2f9d48", "parents": ["453c6d45269bb39aa0e58afa7942d0aa5cec49bc"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Butkovits Atila \u003cabutkovits@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1729482 - disable browser_storage_fission_local_storage.js on Linux_debug for frequent failures. a=RyanVM DONTBUILD", "files": ["devtools/client/storage/test/browser.ini"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "bcd0649ee33329c543b91f9ec66de31d3dee4694", "parents": ["32173ce051143f88f26c0888fb164b3c4c2f9d48"], "tags": []}], "date": 1640102168, "git_changesets": [null, null], "user": "abutkovits@mozilla.com"}, "131": {"changesets": [{"author": "ffxbld \u003cffxbld@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "No Bug, mozilla-esr91 repo-update HSTS HPKP remote-settings tld-suffixes - a=repo-update r=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D134944", "files": ["netwerk/dns/effective_tld_names.dat", "security/manager/ssl/StaticHPKPins.h", "security/manager/ssl/nsSTSPreloadList.inc", "services/settings/dumps/security-state/intermediates.json"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "2bdd50218ba56ffa5080f3b3de59699052ebb4ad", "parents": ["bcd0649ee33329c543b91f9ec66de31d3dee4694"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Lee Salzman \u003clsalzman@mozilla.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1722054 - Restructure SwCompositeThread synchronization to not rely on job count. r=jrmuizel, a=RyanVM\n\nThis patch aims to address a worst-case theoretical possibility where the job count might for\nsome reason get out of sync, causing either the SwComposite thread or the main thread to deadlock\nwaiting on jobs that may never become available.\n\nTo this end, we get rid of the job count tracking entirely, and instead just track whether,\nfirst, the SwComposite thread has completed all the jobs that have been queued for it, and,\nsecond, that the main thread, having completed all jobs that were available, is waiting for\njobs to be available or completed such that the SwComposite thread would need to wake it up.\nThe main thread does not need to wait if it knows the SwComposite thread completed all jobs,\nand the SwComposite thread does not need to signal if it knows the main thread is not waiting.\n\nOtherwise stated, so long as both the main and SwComposite threads know there are no more\navailable jobs, then there is no way compositing can advance any further, and so compositing\nmust be finished. This avoids relying on having a job count that is always accurate to track\ntermination.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D121821", "files": ["gfx/wr/webrender/src/compositor/sw_compositor.rs"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "05a17e57d0fc9e0e74917fc951e5468ed5275aab", "parents": ["2bdd50218ba56ffa5080f3b3de59699052ebb4ad"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Valentin Gosu \u003cvalentin.gosu@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1733274 - Skip CORP check for TYPE_SAVEAS_DOWNLOAD. r=Gijs, a=RyanVM\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D129395", "files": ["netwerk/protocol/http/HttpBaseChannel.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "a4283d730e7c3f174d0e3efd37494676ab6b09cf", "parents": ["05a17e57d0fc9e0e74917fc951e5468ed5275aab"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740847 - part 1: Track split point at replacing collapsible white-spaces. r=m_kato, a=RyanVM\n\nIt `pointToSplit` should be tracked at replacing text, but I have no idea how\nto test this because it replaces the text after the split point.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D131036", "files": ["editor/libeditor/WSRunObject.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "38ff66d6c922c219d4f6c708b3129ca29124dc50", "parents": ["a4283d730e7c3f174d0e3efd37494676ab6b09cf"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740847 - part 2: Make `WhiteSpaceVisibilityKeeper::InsertBRElement()` track insert position in smaller block. r=m_kato, a=RyanVM\n\nAnd also invisible white-space range and replacing white-space position should\nalso be tracked too.\n\nDepends on D131036\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D131037", "files": ["editor/libeditor/EditorDOMPoint.h", "editor/libeditor/SelectionState.h", "editor/libeditor/WSRunObject.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "255cad36ba4d403ae583fe1b51a4fb3ec07d3469", "parents": ["38ff66d6c922c219d4f6c708b3129ca29124dc50"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Masayuki Nakano \u003cmasayuki@d-toybox.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1740847 - part 3: Make `WhiteSpaceVisibilityKeeper::ReplaceText()` track insert position in smaller block. r=m_kato, a=RyanVM\n\nDue to the change of bug 1727844 and bug 1724650, only \"part 3\" cannot be\ngrafted cleanly.\n\nDifferential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D134591", "files": ["editor/libeditor/WSRunObject.cpp"], "git_node": null, "git_parents": [null], "node": "ed25aa724fba406d04e1332d6040ebd629fda893", "parents": ["255cad36ba4d403ae583fe1b51a4fb3ec07d3469"], "tags": []}, {"author": "Bob Owen \u003cbobowencode@gmail.com\u003e", "branch": "default", "desc": "Bug 1664149: Hold a self reference in nsDataObj. r=smaug, a=RyanVM", "files": ["widget/windows/nsDataObj.cpp", "widget/windows/nsDataObj.h"], "git_node": null, "git